---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Editorial Policy & Reference Standards | Real BMI"
    description="Read our editorial policy for evidence-based health content, peer-reviewed methodology, clinical screening definitions, and transparent user guidance."
>
    <Navbar />
    <PageShell
      title="Editorial Policy"
      eyebrow="Methodology & Transparency"
      description="How Bhawanshi Dosi researches, references, and maintains evidence-based health tools and educational content."
      returnUrl="/en/"
      returnLabel="Home"
    >
        <p>Welcome to <strong>Real BMI</strong>. This educational website is run by <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> in Banswara, Rajasthan, India. Our goal is to provide clear, reliable health calculators for everyone. We help you check your body mass index, resting calories, daily burn, and other key body numbers.</p>

        <h2>1. Evidence-Based Guidelines</h2>
        <p>All formulas and health ranges on our site come from trusted global health groups. These include:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>World Health Organization (WHO):</strong> Global obesity cutoffs, Asian BMI ranges (23.0 kg/m²), and waist-to-hip ratio guides.</li>
          <li><strong>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC):</strong> Adult BMI formulas and child growth percentile charts.</li>
          <li><strong>National Institutes of Health (NIH):</strong> Body surface area and metabolic burn formulas.</li>
          <li><strong>Published Medical Research:</strong> Proven math formulas from scientists like Mifflin-St Jeor, Harris-Benedict, Boer, Devine, and Mosteller.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>2. Author Identity &amp; Standards</h2>
        <p>Real BMI is an independent website run with full openness:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Founder &amp; Developer:</strong> <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> manages all coding, formula math, unit tests, and website design. No personal data is ever saved or shared.</li>
          <li><strong>Tested Formulas:</strong> Each calculator is a clean implementation of published health math. We test both metric and imperial units with automated code checks.</li>
          <li><strong>Non-Clinical Resource:</strong> Real BMI is an educational website. It is not a clinic, hospital, or doctor review board. Our calculators provide general health awareness and do not replace medical advice.</li>
          <li><strong>Direct User Feedback:</strong> We welcome questions, math corrections, and research papers from readers and doctors through our contact page.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Openness &amp; Regular Updates</h2>
        <p>We review health guidelines often. When health groups update their guidelines, we update our calculators and guides to match. Each article lists its citations and sources clearly.</p>

        <h2>4. Independent &amp; Ad-Safe Content</h2>
        <p>Real BMI is an independent project. No drug companies or advertisers tell us what to write. Our math remains fair and objective.</p>

        <h2>5. Educational Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>All results on this site are for learning and planning only. We do not offer medical diagnosis, treatments, or prescriptions. Always speak with your doctor or healthcare provider about any health concern.</p>

        <h2>6. Review Cycle &amp; Fact Checks</h2>
        <p>We check all formulas and tables twice a year. When groups like the WHO or CDC publish new data, we check our tools against their whitepapers. We run automated tests before every release to guarantee math precision.</p>

        <h2>7. Human Authorship</h2>
        <p>All guides, worked examples, step-by-step math steps, and FAQs are written originally by Bhawanshi Dosi using primary health sources.</p>

        <h2>8. Corrections Policy</h2>
        <p>We care about accuracy. If you spot a math mistake, an unclear term, or an old link, please tell us on our contact page. We review all reports quickly and update our live code.</p>

        <h2>9. Content Review &amp; Privacy Checks</h2>
        <p>Every calculator and guide goes through four checks before going live:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Step 1: Source check.</strong> We verify formulas against WHO and CDC papers.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 2: Math test.</strong> We test edge cases in both metric and imperial units.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 3: Privacy check.</strong> We make sure no personal data or names are ever collected or stored.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 4: Final review.</strong> We check formatting, links, and text clarity.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </PageShell>
</Layout>
